:null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008090878291582726,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012982795118611855,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.03366,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":22.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.143,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":14.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hagerty, Inc. provides insurance services for collector cars and enthusiast vehicles in the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom. It operates through Insurance and Marketplace segments. The company operates as a managing general agent that underwrites, sells, and services collector car and enthusiast vehicle insurance policies. It also provides Hagerty Drivers Club memberships, which are bundled with insurance policies and give subscribers access to an array of products and services, such as emergency roadside assistance, the Hagerty Drivers Club magazine, special access to automotive enthusiast events, a proprietary vehicle valuation tool, and special vehicle-related discounts; and reinsurance services. In addition, the company offers marketplace services comprising live auctions, online sale platforms, and brokered private sales services where automotive collectors and enthusiasts can buy, sell, and finance collector cars. The company was founded in 1984 and is headquartered in Traverse City, Michigan. Hagerty, Inc. is a subsidiary of Hagerty Holding Corp.","ceo_bio":"Mr. McKeel O. Hagerty | Chairman & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $4.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $770K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 24%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $103K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $10K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Hagerty, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.3B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 32% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $194M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 27\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.04420787318011321},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (86% sell ratio, net $122.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Valued at a 44% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Surging Earnings Estimates Signal Upside for Hagerty (HGTY) Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025824/surging-earnings-estimates-signal-upside-for-hagerty-hgty-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_8-3025824","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793982001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Hagerty (NYSE:HGTY) Stock Price Target Raised at Citizens Jmp","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/hagerty-nysehgty-stock-price-targe